        'Minimal element: 1. Maximal element: 12 — unique here, so 12 is also the maximum.',
        'Chains: $1 \\prec 2 \\prec 4 \\prec 12$ is a longest chain, with 4 elements — the height of the poset. Antichains: $\\{3, 4\\}$ and $\\{4, 6\\}$ are sets of pairwise incomparable elements, and no antichain here has 3 elements, so the width is 2.',
        'Least upper bound of 4 and 6 is 12 (their lcm); greatest lower bound of 4 and 6 is 2 (their gcd).',
